  style.font-color: "#344D67"
  style.fill: "#FFFFFF"
  style.font-size: 14
  tooltip: "Append bounded diagnostics for eligible invocations and read the selected retained invocation on explicit log lookup.\nConditions: Primary/advanced recording and retired-command admission bypass the generic logging wrapper; other eligible commands may have file logging disabled or degraded.; The configured log root is selected independently of the record --root and installation working directory. This aggregate access describes distinct append and lookup paths, not a requirement that each invocation reads and writes logs."
}
n_706c6163656d656e743a4d4f442d3031313a70657273697374656e63653a52656769737465726564206f7065726174696f6e616c207265636f726473 -- n_706c6163656d656e743a4d4f442d3031313a70657273697374656e63653a5265636f7264207472616e73616374696f6e206d65746164617461: "disjoint locations" {
  tooltip: "Authoritative records and private transaction state remain separate; Private locks, epochs, and journals coordinate storage and exact recovery without becoming registered engineering records or workflow authority.; The record operation has selected and validated one project root and change. Current source addresses authoritative files under docs/changes/{change_id} and private coordination under .rigorloop/record-store/{change_id}.; Disjoint describes those declared path-containment scopes; it does not assert different devices, users, hosts, or immunity from all filesystem aliases."
  style.stroke: "#987335"
  style.font-color: "#725321"
  style.fill: "#FFFFFF"
  style.stroke-dash: 3
  style.font-size: 14
}
n_706c6163656d656e743a4d4f442d3031343a6465706c6f796d656e743a53656c65637465642074617267657420736b696c6c20756e697473 -- n_706c6163656d656e743a4d4f442d3031343a6465706c6f796d656e743a52657461696e656420696e7374616c6c6174696f6e206f726967696e616c73: "disjoint locations" {
  tooltip: "Retained originals stay outside skill discovery; Original content and transient candidate bytes must not become discoverable skill instructions or overwrite unrelated target units.; For real installation, installCandidate creates a private retention directory beneath the invoking project and rejects overlap with supported and retained discovery roots.; The relation compares the selected target unit scope and retention scope; their common project context does not merge them or authorize replacement of shared parents."
  style.stroke: "#987335"
  style.font-color: "#725321"
  style.fill: "#FFFFFF"
  style.stroke-dash: 3
  style.font-size: 14
}
n_706c6163656d656e743a4d4f442d3031343a6465706c6f796d656e743a53656c65637465642074617267657420736b696c6c20756e697473 -- n_706c6163656d656e743a4d4f442d3031343a6465706c6f796d656e743a52657461696e656420696e7374616c6c6174696f6e206f726967696e616c73: "same filesystem" {
  tooltip: "Installation targets and retention use one filesystem; The inspected replacement mechanism uses guarded rename and hard-link publication with retained originals, requiring same-filesystem placement.; Before detaching an original, installCandidate compares the selected target parent device with the pinned retention directory device and rejects cross-filesystem placement.; The relation applies to the active target selected for that invocation. Descriptor-relative operations and destination safety checks still apply; no general platform compatibility is inferred."
  style.stroke: "#987335"
  style.font-color: "#725321"
  style.fill: "#FFFFFF"
  style.stroke-dash: 3
  style.font-size: 14
}
